	(descr "ALINX AC7200 XC7A200T-2FBG484I FPGA SOM footprint for the CARRIER board it plugs into (mates CON1-4 with Panasonic AXK680337YG headers). Board outline (55.00 x 45.00mm, confirmed BOTH by the user's reference 3D model AND ALINX's own dimensioned manual drawing), 4x mounting holes, and all 4 connectors' real center position + rotation extracted from the user's reference 3D model (pcb/single_fpga/cad/AC7200.3.0.stp) by tracing its real STEP AP214 assembly structure by hand. Pin-by-pin signal names (see the companion AC7200.kicad_sym) cross-checked against ALINX's own real user manual (docs/AC7200_User_Manual.pdf) -- see that symbol's Description for the one correction applied (CON1 pin 27, a real duplicate/typo in ALINX's own document). Per-connector PAD geometry is the real Panasonic AXK680337YG land pattern (pad 0.25x0.75mm, 40 pins/row at 0.5mm pitch, rows staggered by 0.25mm -- see the standalone AXK680337YG library footprint), reused here 4x at each connector's real center position + rotation, replacing the earlier 0.3x1.0mm estimate. Mounting hole diameter (2.7mm) is ASSUMED M2.5 clearance, matching this project's own standoff convention elsewhere (pcb/layout_multi_fpga.py's STANDOFF_HOLE_NAME) -- not confirmed for this specific module.")
	(tags "ALINX AC7200 XC7A200T FPGA SOM Artix-7")
